---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<Layout title="The Pipeline">
  <h1>The pipeline</h1>
  <p>
    The safe rehearsal separates implemented build gates from agent capabilities that still need
    to be verified. Its release path, after explicit approval, is:
  </p>
  <pre>Proposed change → PR review → Manual approved merge →
GitHub Actions (build + supply-chain security + deploy) → GitHub Pages (live site)</pre>
  <p>Automatic code review has been demonstrated independently. The following pages explain the capabilities and their current limits:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><a href={`${base}capabilities/copilot-code-review/`}>Copilot Code Review</a> — AI review when configured and eligible</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}capabilities/agent-merge/`}>Agent Merge</a> — not verified in this rehearsal; ordinary auto-merge is different</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}capabilities/github-actions/`}>GitHub Actions (CI/CD)</a> — builds, gates, and deploys</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}capabilities/security-review/`}>AI-assisted security review</a> — the supply-chain layer: dependencies, secrets, tokens</li>
    <li><a href={`${base}capabilities/lifecycle-automation/`}>End-to-end lifecycle automation</a> — distinguish working checks from unproven steps</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    See <a href={`${base}secure-supply-chain/`}>Secure your supply chain</a> for why the
    security beats in this demo live in dependencies and CI/CD, not just application code.
  </p>
</Layout>
